  "notes": "Canon CR3 raw files as input.\n\n## Added\n- **CR3 input.** Canon CR3 raw files convert to every output format \u2014 WebP, AVIF, JPEG XL and HEIC. They are developed by LibRaw the way `dcraw_emu -w -o 1 -6 -g 2.4 12.92` would: the camera's white balance, sRGB colour, 16 bits per sample, turned the way the camera was held. A camera LibRaw does not yet support is refused with a message naming it, rather than converted with the wrong colours.\n\n## Known limitations\n- A CR3's Exif is not carried into the output yet.\n- No lens corrections: distortion and vignetting the camera would correct in its own JPEGs stay in the picture.\n\n## Fixed\n- Dependency updates closing every open security advisory that has a fix (rustls, rustls-webpki, esbuild and the frontend's npm packages).\n\nLibRaw is used unmodified under CDDL-1.0; its notice is in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Installers for Windows, macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel) and Linux are attached by the release workflow; existing installs update themselves."
